From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: a buffer that cannot fit the budget reclaims or over-budgets, not abort

Ported from Frizti/Fritchii 464fbb45b, shipped in Fritchii v5.2 as "No more crash when the PC's
memory budget is reached during long sessions (seen in Castle Town after half an hour). Buffers in
system memory may now go over Windows' budget, like textures already could."

That is this port's oldest open symptom: sessions that die instead of continuing. Our own records
have a 34-minute death, and an older log with 72 "Out of device memory" events and the texture
thresholds walked down to their floor.

Two changes, both in the buffer path:

- MemoryAllocator::CreateBuffer, when vmaCreateBuffer answers out of memory and the usage is not
  MemoryUsage::DeviceLocal, retries once with VMA_ALLOCATION_CREATE_WITHIN_BUDGET_BIT cleared, and
  logs whether the buffer was made anyway. For host memory the budget is a soft hint - exceeding it
  pages, while refusing aborted the emulator. Device-local allocations keep the budget, because there
  the budget is real.
- StagingBufferPool::CreateStagingBuffer catches the allocation failure, drops every staging buffer
  that is not deferred and whose tick the GPU has passed, resets each level's two indices, and tries
  once more. So a fragmented pool reclaims before it gives up.

What this can break. A host-memory allocation that goes over budget can make the process page, so a
session that used to abort can now stall until the OS frees something - slower, but alive, which is
the intended trade. The eviction pass resets iterate_index and delete_index for every level it
touches, so those lists are re-walked from the start; that is what the pool does after any release.

Measured or a guess: upstream's comment names the exact failure - a texture upload in Ocarina's town
square after 36 minutes - and their build shipped it. Ours is the same buffer path from the same
lineage, and our own logs show the out-of-memory class. No console has run this build.

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_staging_buffer_pool.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_staging_buffer_pool.cpp
index f6f66674de..64647ec7d4 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_staging_buffer_pool.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_staging_buffer_pool.cpp
@@ -359,7 +359,29 @@ StagingBufferRef StagingBufferPool::CreateStagingBuffer(size_t size, MemoryUsage
     if (device.IsBufferDeviceAddressSupported()) {
         buffer_ci.usage |= VK_BUFFER_USAGE_SHADER_DEVICE_ADDRESS_BIT;
     }
-    vk::Buffer buffer = memory_allocator.CreateBuffer(buffer_ci, usage);
+    vk::Buffer buffer;
+    try {
+        buffer = memory_allocator.CreateBuffer(buffer_ci, usage);
+    } catch (const vk::Exception& e) {
+        // Out of memory: free every idle staging buffer and try once more.
+        size_t freed = 0;
+        for (StagingBuffersCache* cache : {&device_local_cache, &upload_cache, &download_cache}) {
+            for (StagingBuffers& level : *cache) {
+                const size_t before = level.entries.size();
+                std::erase_if(level.entries, [this](const StagingBuffer& entry) {
+                    return !entry.deferred && scheduler.IsFree(entry.tick);
+                });
+                freed += before - level.entries.size();
+                level.iterate_index = 0;
+                level.delete_index = 0;
+            }
+        }
+        LOG_WARNING(Render_Vulkan,
+                    "Staging buffer of {} MiB could not be made ({}); freed {} idle staging "
+                    "buffers and retrying",
+                    buffer_ci.size >> 20, e.what(), freed);
+        buffer = memory_allocator.CreateBuffer(buffer_ci, usage);
+    }
     if (device.HasDebuggingToolAttached()) {
         ++buffer_index;
         buffer.SetObjectNameEXT(fmt::format("Staging Buffer {}", buffer_index).c_str());
diff --git a/src/video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_memory_allocator.cpp b/src/video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_memory_allocator.cpp
index 488f4a776d..52c5f2ba66 100644
--- a/src/video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_memory_allocator.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_memory_allocator.cpp
@@ -448,7 +448,22 @@ vk::Buffer MemoryAllocator::CreateBuffer(const VkBufferCreateInfo &ci, MemoryUsa
     VkMemoryPropertyFlags property_flags{};
 
     if (!CreateBufferInSeparatePool(ci, usage, alloc_ci, handle, allocation, alloc_info)) {
-        vk::Check(vmaCreateBuffer(allocator, &ci, &alloc_ci, &handle, &allocation, &alloc_info));
+        VkResult result =
+            vmaCreateBuffer(allocator, &ci, &alloc_ci, &handle, &allocation, &alloc_info);
+        // Staging buffers live in system memory, where the budget is the OS's soft hint: going over
+        // it pages, while refusing aborted the emulator - a texture upload in Ocarina's town square
+        // after 36 minutes. Device-local buffers keep the budget, because there it is real.
+        if ((result == VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY || result == VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY) &&
+            usage != MemoryUsage::DeviceLocal) {
+            VmaAllocationCreateInfo over_budget = alloc_ci;
+            over_budget.flags &= ~VMA_ALLOCATION_CREATE_WITHIN_BUDGET_BIT;
+            result =
+                vmaCreateBuffer(allocator, &ci, &over_budget, &handle, &allocation, &alloc_info);
+            LOG_WARNING(Render_Vulkan, "Buffer of {} KiB (usage {}) over the memory budget: {}",
+                        ci.size >> 10, static_cast<u32>(usage),
+                        result == VK_SUCCESS ? "made anyway" : "failed");
+        }
+        vk::Check(result);
     }
     vmaGetAllocationMemoryProperties(allocator, allocation, &property_flags);
 
